cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EBBEF2p in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "EBBEF2p: Euler-Bernoulli beams on two-parameter elastic foundations"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Teodoru
    given-names: Iancu-Bogdan
    email: bteodoru@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Gheorghe Asachi Technical University of Iași"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8298-9374"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-26
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bteodoru/ebbef2p-python"
url: "https://ebbef2p-python.readthedocs.io"
abstract: >-
  EBBEF2p is a Python finite element package for the static analysis of
  Euler-Bernoulli beams on Winkler, Pasternak and modified Vlasov
  foundations, with foundation parameters varying along the beam, soil
  continuing beyond the beam ends, and soil pressure including the
  concentrated forces of the shear layer.
keywords:
  - finite element method
  - beam on elastic foundation
  - two-parameter foundation
  - Pasternak
  - modified Vlasov model
  - soil-structure interaction
  - geotechnical engineering
